@1=~%name%'s Body~
@2=~This is the dead body of %name%.

STATISTICS:

Weight: %weight%
~

@3=~Without enough of the body being present, the spell failed.~
@4=~%raise% This spell will fail if the body is not present.~
@5=~%res% This spell works even if the body is not present.~
@6=~%desc% If succesful the raised character will suffer a reduction in constiution by one.~ 
@7=~%name%'s Decaying Body~
@8=~This is the dead body of %name%. It has deteriorated beyond the ability to be used for the Raise Dead spell. Only Resurrection will allow a body in this state to be restored to life.

STATISTICS:

Weight: %weight%
~
@9=~%name%'s Body has decayed beyond usefulness for Raise Dead and similar spells.~
@10=~%raise% After ten days following death the body will have deteriorated such that this spell will no longer work.~
@11=~%res% Resurrection will work any length of time after death.~
@12=~%name% has been dead too long for revivify to work~
@13=~Revifify~
@14=~Revivify
(Necromancy)

Level: 3
Sphere: Necromantic 
Range: Visual range of the caster
Duration: Permanent 
Casting Time: 9 
Area of Effect: 1 person 
Saving Throw: Special 
Revivify allows the priest to restore life to a member of their party as long as they have been dead for no longer than one minute. 
The party member will be restored with only one hit point.
This spell requires the body to be intact so that it is not effective for disentegrated, dismembered or incinerated allies. This spell will fail if the body is not present.~
@15=~Revivify is only effective within one minute of death~
@100=~Main Component~
@200=~Raise Dead Level Drain Penalty/Resurrection Con Penalty~
@300=~Progressive price for Raise Dead spell~
@400=~Time limits for Raise Dead and similar spells~
@500=~Add revivify- 3rd level spell that allows NPCs to be raised within one minute of death~
@600=~Temple Resurrection of Fallen Companions~
@601=~I carry the body of a fallen companion. Can your temple restore them to life?~
@602=~I sense you carry the weight of death with you. The temple can restore your companion to life. Present the body and I shall perform the rite. Raise Dead costs gold equal to the companion's level multiplied by 1000. Resurrection, for bodies that have decayed, costs 10,000 gold.~
@603=~I have multiple fallen companions. Which shall I restore?~
@604=~You do not carry the body of that companion.~
@605=~This body has decayed beyond the ability of Raise Dead to restore. Only Resurrection can help, for a cost of 10,000 gold. Shall I proceed?~
@606=~Restoration complete. %name% has been returned to life. They await you outside the temple.~
@607=~I cannot afford the temple's services.~
@608=~The temple's rite is complete. %name% has been restored to life. Speak with them and they may rejoin your party.~
@609=~You do not carry any bodies of fallen companions.~
@610=~I am sorry, but the temple requires payment for its services. Return when you have the necessary gold.~
@620=~Temple Resurrection requires either the Time Limits (400) or Revivify (500) component to be installed.~
